#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128801 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "82248f5b-84f1-5acf-ade8-4ed90a410cc3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12530" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses $m_1=1\\,\\textrm{kg}$, $m_2=2\\,\\textrm{kg}$, $m_3=3\\,\\textrm{kg}$, and $m_4=3\\,\\textrm{kg}$ located at $x_1=-1\\,\\textrm{m}$, $x_2 = 1\\,\\textrm{m}$, $x_3 = 3\\,\\textrm{m}$, and $x_4 = 5 \\, \\textrm{m}$, respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}m_{1} &= 1, & m_{2}|= 2, & m_{3}|= 3, & m_{4}|= 3, \\\\ x_{1}|=-1, & x_{2}|= 1, & x_{3}|= 3, & x_{4}|= 5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{O} &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)m_{i}x_{i} \\\\\n&= m_{1}x_{1} + m_{2}x_{2} + m_{3}x_{3} + m_{4}x_{4} \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (-1) + 2 \\cdot 1 + 3 \\cdot 3 + 3 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-1 + 2 + 9 + 15 \\\\\n&= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $25\\,\\textrm{kg} \\cdot \\textrm{m}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128802 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "adcc17f7-7acf-50fd-bb68-b9e6b0477fe3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12531" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2026/Source/Images/7d1080a4e47e1448ba5bd6fef71f207e.png)" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overline{x}$, of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O$.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}m_{1} &= 2, & m_{2}|= 4, & m_{3}|= 3, \\\\ x_{1}|=-1, & x_{2}|= 2, & x_{3}|= 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)m_{i} \\\\\n&= m_{1} + m_{2} + m_{3} \\\\\n&= 2 + 4 + 3 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{O} &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)m_{i}x_{i} \\\\\n&= m_{1}x_{1} + m_{2}x_{2} + m_{3}x_{3} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot (-1) + 4 \\cdot 2 + 3 \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&=-2 + 8 + 12 \\\\\n&= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{18}{9}=2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128803 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "0f13ad0c-9523-542d-a3bf-c562f09d6a88" :question/math-academy-id "e-12532" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})$, what is the value of $\\overline{y}$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2026/Source/Images/a98849cc62e6b254955495d1c98f4f85.png)" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $(x_1y_1),(x_2,y_2),\\ldots,(x_n,y_n)$ on the plane is given by\n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left(\\dfrac{M_y}{m},\\dfrac{M_x}{m}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i y_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\nm_1 = 3, \\qquad m_2 = 5, \\qquad m_3 = 1\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\ny_1 = 3, \\qquad y_2 = 0, \\qquad y_3 = 3\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)m_{i} \\\\\n&= m_{1} + m_{2} + m_{3} \\\\\n&= 3 + 5 + 1 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{x} &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)m_{i}y_{i} \\\\\n&= m_{1}y_{1} + m_{2}y_{2} + m_{3}y_{3} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 3 + 5 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 9 + 0 + 3 \\\\\n&= 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{12}{9} = \\dfrac{4}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128804 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/id #uuid "ae5cebdd-4eb8-5eed-9b89-fffb153c844b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12533" :question/problem "Two point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $10\\,\\rm{lb}$ and is $4\\,\\rm{ft}$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2026/Source/Images/ce815ce5a9571e39d171d6fccd5e66bf.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $A$.\nThe length of the rod is $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,\\rm{ft}$. So, the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is\n\n$$\n9 - 4 = 5\\,\\rm{ft}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2026/Source/Images/5fbffe1d0b5c5d2ef8b9c2618163c14b.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m \\cdot 5 = -5m\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $10 \\cdot 4 = 40\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n40 - 5m &= 0 \\\\\n5m &= 40 \\\\\nm &= 8lb\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af761a85-e4c8-5b27-81e9-97aca3773e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126669} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d5582b-4fec-5a73-8df1-d30026074e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126670} {:answer/id #uuid "c2575e83-b836-5df6-95db-e86cf00f8200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{50}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126671} {:answer/id #uuid "5c71ca70-8238-51cf-95aa-7b2c9c35b4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126672} {:answer/id #uuid "6149a7cb-85e4-5806-8acf-fa93c8fd3d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{44}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c71ca70-8238-51cf-95aa-7b2c9c35b4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126672} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b287a49-db3e-5d25-8be1-15e012197093" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126668}] :question/id #uuid "581d1406-8e22-5cce-a290-02e4c2d04cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-163082" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2026/Source/Images/q-163082.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1294238-b0cc-5a1d-972b-0b6abfa5d0e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126723} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cfc22e-75d2-5cb1-acdc-04c01405bd43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126724} {:answer/id #uuid "06fda4c4-3073-5e7a-af27-2425381cedb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126725} {:answer/id #uuid "1e761749-3f64-5266-916d-62085fdf5c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126726} {:answer/id #uuid "6ead26d4-7517-595c-804e-6e6a2590d429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e761749-3f64-5266-916d-62085fdf5c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126726} :answer-field/id #uuid "e063d297-fd8c-5e50-bffc-a1c1dda34fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126722}] :question/id #uuid "0c837a8e-f3db-50ec-96a6-565fd7d0b50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163796" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2026/Source/Images/q-163796.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $10kg$ and $8kg$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $5m$, find the distance between the fulcrum and $A$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8546df09-7ac1-5d49-90a0-ad3d968847be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126729} {:answer/id #uuid "c13a915e-cc5a-51aa-b88f-1effb98464e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126730} {:answer/id #uuid "c51de018-ac34-548d-921a-9ed25e54bebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126731} {:answer/id #uuid "290f70fa-9f21-55c8-a9d2-9be9801c94bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126732} {:answer/id #uuid "345aa25e-2ca4-5467-befd-a8c3ebeec36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "345aa25e-2ca4-5467-befd-a8c3ebeec36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126733} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6bf9b21-23a6-59b7-8c28-fa03a626adcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126728}] :question/id #uuid "a0d6fe0c-2d8e-592e-808b-507c87fc4991" :question/math-academy-id "q-163797" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2026/Source/Images/q-163797.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $10m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $3kg$ and is $4m$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A$."}]}
